        "category_TJTW8G": {
          "type": "category",
          "settings": {
            "category_id": "max-relief",
            "category_name": "Max Relief",
            "icon": "🧴",
            "question_count": 7,
            "open_first": false,
            "q_1": "Will the CBD show up on a drug test?",
            "a_1": "<p>No. Max Relief is a topical — it doesn't enter the bloodstream in meaningful amounts. Full spectrum CBD in topical form does not produce a positive drug test under standard testing protocols. If you have specific concerns about testing for a competition or employer, consult your testing authority directly.</p>",
            "q_2": "How quickly does it work?",
            "a_2": "<p>Most users feel the cooling effect from menthol within 3–5 minutes and the nerve block effect from Lidocaine within 5–10 minutes. The anti-inflammatory benefits from CBD, Arnica, and Turmeric build over 20–30 minutes. With repeated use, the capsaicin component desensitizes pain receptors — it becomes more effective over time, not less.</p>",
            "q_3": "What's different about Max Relief vs Voltaren or IcyHot?",
            "a_3": "<p>Voltaren contains one active ingredient (diclofenac — anti-inflammatory only). IcyHot contains one mechanism (counterirritant only). Max Relief combines four simultaneous pathways: pharmaceutical nerve block (Lidocaine HCl), counterirritant (Menthol + Capsaicin), anti-inflammatory (1200mg CBD + Arnica + Turmeric), and circulation support (Clary Sage). No other OTC product does all four.</p>",
            "q_4": "Is it safe for daily use?",
            "a_4": "<p>Yes. Max Relief is formulated for daily use. The Lidocaine HCl concentration is within OTC-safe limits. The CBD is non-intoxicating and topical only. We recommend applying to the affected area 2–3 times daily or as needed. Avoid contact with eyes and mucous membranes.</p>",
            "q_5": "Jar or Stick — which should I get?",
            "a_5": "<p>The Stick (30ml) is better for targeted application — precise, no mess, easy to carry in a gym bag. The Jar (60ml) gives you more product for larger areas like lower back, quads, or shoulders, and is better value for daily users. Most frequent users prefer the Jar.</p>",
            "q_6": "Is Max Relief suitable for post-surgery recovery?",
            "a_6": "<p>Many of our customers use Max Relief during post-surgery rehabilitation. However, always consult with your surgeon or physiotherapist before using any topical product on or near a surgical site. Don't apply to open wounds or freshly sutured skin.</p>",
            "q_7": "Can I use Max Relief alongside prescription pain medication?",
            "a_7": "<p>Max Relief is a topical with minimal systemic absorption. However, if you're on prescription medication or have a medical condition, consult your healthcare provider before use. We cannot provide specific medical advice.</p>",
