        "category_3fkRME": {
          "type": "category",
          "settings": {
            "category_id": "electro",
            "category_name": "Electro+ Drops",
            "icon": "💧",
            "question_count": 6,
            "open_first": false,
            "q_1": "Does it taste like anything?",
            "a_1": "<p><strong>Does it taste like anything? </strong>+Barely. At the recommended dose you'll notice a very slight saltiness — that's it. No sweetness, no bitterness, no chemical aftertaste. It won't change the taste of your coffee, water, or shake. This is the biggest feedback we get from people who've switched from LMNT or Liquid IV — those products have a strong, sweet flavor that dominates your drink. Electro+ doesn't.</p>",
            "q_2": "How many drops per serving?",
            "a_2": "<p>Start with 1 full dropper (approximately 1ml) in 16oz of water. Most people find 2–3 droppers optimal on training days or in hot weather. Because it's a concentrate with no sweeteners, you can freely adjust your dose without it tasting overwhelming. Experiment to find what works for you.</p>",
            "q_3": "Is the 4oz bottle worth it over the 1oz?",
            "a_3": "<p>The 4oz is $45 for 120 servings — $0.38 per serving. The 1oz is $25 for 30 servings — $0.83 per serving. If you plan to use it daily, the 4oz saves you significant money over time and means less frequent reordering. If you've never tried it, the 1oz is a sensible way to test it first. The 30-day guarantee means either choice is risk-free.</p>",
            "q_4": "Can I use Electro+ while pregnant or breastfeeding?",
            "a_4": "<p>Consult your healthcare provider before using any supplement while pregnant or breastfeeding. While Electro+ contains only natural trace minerals, every pregnancy is different and your doctor is best positioned to advise based on your specific situation.</p>",
            "q_5": "Where do the minerals come from?",
            "a_5": "<p>Electro+ minerals are derived from <strong>natural Salt Lake Brine </strong>— one of the most mineral-dense natural sources on earth. Salt lake brines are naturally concentrated over millennia, resulting in an exceptionally rich mineral profile. The brine is filtered, purified, and concentrated before bottling. This gives you over 50 trace minerals in their naturally occurring ionic form — how your body absorbs them most effectively — without any synthetic mineral additions.</p>",
            "q_6": "Does Electro+ contain iodine?",
            "a_6": "<p><strong>Does Electro+ contain iodine? </strong>+Yes, in trace amounts as it naturally occurs in the Salt Lake Brine source. If you have a thyroid condition or are iodine-sensitive, consult your healthcare provider before use.</p>",
