        "category_LXaUQW": {
          "type": "category",
          "settings": {
            "category_id": "perform",
            "category_name": "Perform+",
            "icon": "💊",
            "question_count": 8,
            "open_first": false,
            "q_1": "Will Perform+ get me banned from sport?",
            "a_1": "<p>No. β-Ecdysterone is not on the WADA prohibited list and is not banned by USADA, UFC, or any major sports organization. WADA added it to their monitoring list in 2021 — but monitoring is distinct from prohibited. Athletes are only sanctioned for substances on the prohibited list. Every batch of Perform+ is 3rd party tested to confirm zero contamination with banned substances.</p>",
            "q_2": "How long before I see results?",
            "a_2": "<p>The primary WADA-funded study ran 10 weeks and found up to +2kg lean muscle gained vs placebo, plus significant bench press strength improvements. Most users report noticeably faster recovery within 2 weeks and visible strength gains by weeks 4–6. The full anabolic effect builds over time — which is why the 60-cap option is recommended as your first order.</p>",
            "q_3": "Do I need to do post-cycle therapy (PCT)?",
            "a_3": "<p>No. β-Ecdysterone is completely non-hormonal — it activates the Akt/mTOR muscle protein synthesis pathway without binding to androgen or estrogen receptors. It doesn't suppress your natural testosterone production. There is no hormonal rebound to manage. Take it continuously or stop whenever you choose.</p>",
            "q_4": "Is Perform+ safe for women?",
            "a_4": "<p>Yes — and female athletes may benefit more from Perform+ than most performance supplements precisely because it's non-hormonal. Zero testosterone increase, no masculinizing effects, no hair loss, no voice changes, no menstrual disruption. The muscle protein synthesis pathway it activates works identically regardless of biological sex.</p>",
            "q_5": "How does it compare to peptides like BPC-157 or SARMs?",
            "a_5": "<p>Completely different category. Peptides and SARMs require injections, grey-market sourcing, carry legal risk in competitive sports, and most have limited human clinical data. β-Ecdysterone has more published human research than most peptides being discussed in performance communities. It's oral, legal, non-hormonal, and 3rd party tested. Try the legal, clinically-studied option first.</p>",
            "q_6": "What's the cyclodextrin complex and why does it matter?",
            "a_6": "<p>Ecdysterone has poor water solubility — meaning raw ecdysterone powder absorbs poorly. Cyclodextrin is a cyclic sugar molecule used in pharmaceutical drug delivery that forms an inclusion complex around the ecdysterone molecule, dramatically increasing solubility and cellular uptake. Our 1:4 ratio means 250mg of ecdysterone per 1250mg total capsule fill. Most budget brands skip this step entirely.</p>",
            "q_7": "Why 60 capsules instead of 30 as a first order?",
            "a_7": "<p>The WADA study that produced the +2kg lean muscle result ran for 10 weeks. One bottle gives you 30 days — enough to feel a difference, but not the full research timeline. Two bottles gives you 60 days, puts you into the period where the most significant results were observed, and saves $13 vs two separate purchases ($98 vs $85). If you want results that match the research — give it the time the research used.</p>",
            "q_8": "Can I take Perform+ with other supplements?",
            "a_8": "<p>Yes. Perform+ stacks cleanly with creatine, protein, pre-workouts, and the other PHASIS products (Max Relief and Electro+). Because it's non-stimulant and non-hormonal, there are no known interactions with common supplements. If you're taking prescription medication, consult your healthcare provider.</p>",
            "q_9": "",
            "a_9": "",
